r":null},{"season":2025,"team":"CHI","distance":0.7175,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Ben Johnson"},{"season":2025,"team":"BUF","distance":0.725,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Joe Brady"}],"defense":[{"season":2023,"team":"NYG","distance":0.8443,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"NYG","distance":0.9029,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"ARI","distance":1.539,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Vance Joseph"},{"season":2024,"team":"DET","distance":1.638,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Aaron Glenn"},{"season":2024,"team":"DEN","distance":1.828,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Vance Joseph"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Vikings are 6-0 through week 7 of the 2026 season and have outscored opponents 125 to 74. The defense has done most of the work, ranking 1st in EPA allowed while the offense sits 29th in EPA per play. What sets them apart is the 2nd highest play-action rate and the highest blitz rate in the league.","offense":"The Vikings offense has struggled, ranking 25th or worse in three of the five main efficiency measures. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Schematically, they stand out for the 2nd highest play-action rate and the 3rd most backs in the backfield in the league. Kyler Murray has run the passing game, with T.J. Hockenson leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Vikings have one of the best defenses in the league this season, ranking 5th or better in all five main efficiency measures. Its strongest area has been EPA allowed per play, where it leads the league, and it has no real weak spot. Dallas Turner has been as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise is Blake Cashman, who has 4.5 sacks, after doing little as a pass rusher a year ago. In terms of scheme, they have the highest blitz rate in the league.","special":"The Vikings have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 95% of field goals, which is well above average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into the offensive line, about 31% of the money on the books. Their running backs were among the oldest in the league.","players":"The quarterback job has been split, with Kyler Murray and Carson Wentz both getting meaningful snaps. Targets have been spread around, with T.J. Hockenson and Justin Jefferson leading a group where nobody has more than a fifth of the looks. Aaron Jones has handled most of the work in the backfield with 71% of the carries. On defense, Dallas Turner leads the team with 6 sacks and Byron Murphy has picked off 3 passes.","coaching":"Kevin O'Connell is calling the offense as head coach and Brian Flores is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2023 Titans and the 2024 Ravens under Todd Monken. Their defense looks most like the 2023 and 2022 Giants.","trends":"The offense went from 28th in EPA per play in 2025 to 29th so far this season, about where it was. The defense moved from 4th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 1st so far this season, a modest improvement. The biggest change in approach was pass rate, which went from 58% to 52%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}